{
  "id": "ss.lib.spider-arm",
  "name": "Spider arm",
  "description": "One jointed arm of the spider hand, rooted at the origin and reaching out along +x: a femur up to a raised knee, a tibia back down to the claw, and a hooked tarsus at the end of it. Every plate the weapon owns composes this — the slot icon fans three of them off one knuckle, Eighth Leg fans four, Hauling Arms mirrors two of them inward — so the arm is drawn once and the finds are arrangements of it. What keeps it an animal's leg rather than an armature: the bones are swept along opposite bows so a shallow S runs through the limb, they taper hard instead of stepping down, the tibia carries bristles raked back toward the body, and the foot is a long hook with a short barb opposing it — a grab has a long side and a short one. Bones darken outward the way the Scolopend's fringe does, which is depth rather than light: a limb the parent turns to any angle cannot carry a lit edge without the light turning with it. The weapon's own arms on the field are the same curves solved per frame against a live target, so this is that animal in a pose rather than the sprite drawn there.",
